\p{
    I am an MPhil student in \em{Advanced Computer Science} and a Research Assistant at \ucam, where my research investigates how architecture and verification paradigm influence the performance of large language models on step-wise reasoning verification.
    Prior to the MPhil, I was a Research Assistant at \shailab, contributing to post training methods that connect LLM reasoning with formal languages in pursuit of more transparent and verifiable AI systems.
    I completed my undergraduate degree in \em{Computer Science} at \kcl, graduating with First Class Honours, and I remain part of the Google DeepMind Education Programme cohort.
}


\p{
    My research interests lie in \strong{Natural Language Processing} and the \strong{post training of Large Language Models}, with particular attention to how these models are trained and evaluated when judging the validity of their own reasoning.
    I aim to contribute to verification methods that allow the judgments produced by language models to be trusted, with particular interest in settings where such judgments inform decisions that affect people directly.
}

